# Feature Prompt Template

Use this template to define one feature or story. Generate a feature-specific instance during the define stage and keep it branch-scoped.

## Feature Metadata

- Feature name: Loan Request History
- Branch: feature/loan-history
- Owner: local developer
- Target milestone / release: local validation branch
- Related issue or ticket: PGT

## Business Goal

As a customer, I want to see the history of my loan requests so I can review prior requests and outcomes without relying on incomplete derivation from account or transaction state.

## Problem Statement

The current flow persists the approved loan account and withdrawal transaction but does not retain the original loan request details or the denied outcome. That prevents a customer from reviewing previous loan requests, including denied and failed attempts, using a consistent API contract.

## Scope

### In Scope
- Persist loan request metadata and outcome per customer
- Expose a REST-only history endpoint for customer loan requests
- Update the API contract and local validation artifacts
- Validate with SA, UT, coverage, and functional/API tests

### Out of Scope
- UI or JSP changes
- SOAP contract changes
- Unrelated bug fixes
- Existing SOAtest or Virtualize asset reuse

## Non-Goals

- No UI / JSP / E2E work
- No SOAP contract change
- No fixing pre-existing bugs
- No broad cleanup work not required by this feature

## Locked Decisions

- Decision 1: Persist loan requests in DB; derivation from transaction history is insufficient.
- Decision 2: History is scoped per customer.
- Decision 3: Surface is REST only; no SOAP or UI work in this iteration.
- Decision 4: DTP filter ID is 33.
- Decision 5: New-class coverage target is at least 80%; zero new Sev1 SA violations vs master under builtin://CWE Top 25 + On the Cusp 2025.
- Decision 6: Local runtime uses WSL and port 8081 if 8080 is occupied.

## Functional Requirements

1. Persist each loan request and its outcome for the customer.
2. Return loan request history ordered newest first.
3. Return HTTP 200 with an empty array for a customer with no requests.
4. Return HTTP 404 for an unknown customer.
5. Include request metadata and provider response details in the stored record.

## API / Data Contract

Describe the required external behavior, endpoints, payload shape, validation rules, and response semantics.

- Endpoint(s): GET /customers/{customerId}/loanRequests
- Request contract: path variable customerId
- Response contract: records include id, customerId, requestDate, availableFunds, loanAmount, downPayment, approved, responseDate, loanAccountId, providerName, and message
- Error handling: unknown customer returns 404; provider exception persists FAILED and rethrows the service error
- Persistence requirements: store request before provider call and persist provider outcome for both approved and denied requests
- Ordering or sorting rules: results sort newest first

## Implementation Anchors

- Core code: BankManagerImpl, LoanRequest model/service/DAO, customer loan request handling
- Data layer: schema and migration for persisted loan request data
- REST/UI/API layer: LoanRequestHistoryResource, Swagger definition
- Tests: DAO/service/rest unit tests and generated SOAtest scenarios
- Documentation: swagger.yaml and validation notes

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Loan request history is persisted in the database per customer
- [ ] REST endpoint returns the expected history payload and ordering
- [ ] Unknown customer returns HTTP 404
- [ ] Empty customer history returns HTTP 200 with []
- [ ] SA, UT, and API validation pass against the feature branch
- [ ] Coverage and DTP publish evidence is captured for the new build

## Quality Gates

- Static analysis: run SA on current branch and compare against the new baseline
- Unit tests: pass feature-focused unit tests and regression checks
- Functional/API tests: health and API scenarios pass on the feature branch
- Coverage threshold: new production classes meet or exceed 80% line coverage
- Security / compliance thresholds: no new Sev1 findings under builtin://CWE Top 25 + On the Cusp 2025
- Baseline comparison: compare against fresh DTP baseline on the new server

## Risk / Dependencies

- External dependency 1: new DTP URL and credentials
- Known risk 1: stale Jtest or app coverage data if runs are not cleaned properly
- Required environment or credentials: local WSL app runtime, DTP connection, SOAtest availability

## Validation Evidence Required

- SA report
- UT report and coverage report
- Functional or API report
- Coverage report
- DTP build reference for the new server

## Definition of Done

The feature is complete only when all acceptance criteria are met, all required validation evidence exists, and no blocking quality gate remains unresolved.
